SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The eenndduuttxxeenntt(), ggeettuuttxxeenntt(), ggeettuuttxxiidd(), ggeettuuttxxlliinnee() and sseettuuttxxeenntt()
     functions are expected to conform to IEEE Std 1003.1-2008 (“POSIX.1”).

     The ppuuttuuttxxlliinnee() function deviates from the standard by writing its
     records to multiple database files, depending on its _u_t___t_y_p_e.  This pre‐
     vents the need for special utility functions to update the other data‐
     bases, such as the uuppddllaassttllooggxx() and uuppddwwttmmppxx() functions which are
     available in other implementations.  It also tries to replace
     DEAD_PROCESS entries in the active sessions database when storing
     USER_PROCESS entries and no entry with the same value for _u_t___i_d has been
     found.  The standard always requires a new entry to be allocated, which
     could cause an unbounded growth of the database.

     The ggeettuuttxxuusseerr() and sseettuuttxxddbb() functions, the _u_t___h_o_s_t field of the _u_t_m_p_x
     structure and SHUTDOWN_TIME are extensions.

